meta {
  name: Update Branding
  type: http
  seq: 2
}

put {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/branding
  body: json
  auth: none
}

headers {
  X-Dev-User-ID: {{devUserId}}
  Content-Type: application/json
}

body:json {
  {
    "cta": "#0b5cad",
    "primary": "#1a1a6e",
    "secondary": "#eef3ff",
    "surface": "#f7f7f7",
    "body_text": "#111111",
    "border": "#d0d0d0"
  }
}

docs {
  Replaces the six colours. platform_admin only.

  Validation / behaviour:
    1. Each colour must be #RRGGBB (either case); stored lowercase.
    2. The palette must pass WCAG AA (4.5:1) on eight text pairs: white on
       the CTA colour and its hover shade, white on primary and its hover
       shade, primary on white, primary on secondary, body text on white,
       body text on surface. Otherwise 422 and nothing is stored.
    3. Writes branding.updated to audit_logs with before/after colours.

  Responses:
    200 OK — same body as GET /api/v1/branding
    400 bad_request — body is not JSON
    401 unauthorized / 403 forbidden — not platform_admin
    422 validation_failed — errors[].path is the colour field
        (code invalid_color) or contrast.<pair> (code contrast_too_low);
        details.contrast_failures lists { pair, foreground, background,
        ratio, required } for each failing pair
}
